; The facade's command line, end to end. [Windtrap.run] ends every branch
; in [exit], so half its contract — Law 11's nothing-ran 2, the startup
; refusals' 1, the informational 0 of --help and -l — is only visible to
; a process that waited on it. [suite_main] is that process: a five-test
; suite small enough for the driver to pin whole streams, spawned once
; per scenario with a scrubbed environment. The shape is
; test/mutate_loop's, for the same reason.
;
; Not under @admit, like every other directory whose subject runs where
; no arming reaches it (see ../dune): the code these tests are about
; executes in the child.

(executable
 (name suite_main)
 (modules suite_main)
 (libraries windtrap))

(test
 (name test_facade)
 (modules test_facade)
 (libraries windtrap windtrap_coverage windtrap_instr unix)
 (deps suite_main.exe))
